# What the e2e scripts read from the environment (e2e/README.md). Names and placeholders only: export
# them in your shell, or keep a copy of this outside the repository. No secret belongs here: each pass
# makes its own E2E_AUTH_SECRET.

# An admin URL for the e2e's Postgres: a role that may create databases. The e2e makes and resets its
# own databases beside it (sending_stone_e2e, sending_stone_e2e_0 …), never the app's own.
# local/docker-compose.yaml's server, for example:
E2E_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://admin:password@localhost:5432/postgres

# The module's checkout, at the commit that matches this one (npm ci and npm run test:setup done there).
# Default: fvtt-sending-stone beside this checkout.
SENDING_STONE_MODULE=/path/to/fvtt-sending-stone

# Where Playwright's Chromium is, if not in Playwright's own cache (npm run e2e:browsers puts it there).
# PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/path/to/ms-playwright
